; Surface themes: a named, world-wide look. Painting one (the editor's Themes
; brush) never changes a square's type: an open square takes the floor and
; ceiling, a wall block the wall. The square REFERENCES the theme, so editing
; an entry here repaints every square that uses it (docs/editor-themes-notes.md).
;
; Fields:
;   display   the name the palette shows.
;   floor     the floors.cat id its open squares show.
;   wall      the walls.cat id its wall blocks show.
;   ceiling   the ceilings.cat id its ceilings show.
;   Each is ONE id; an empty or absent one leaves that surface exactly as
;   it is.

[marble_hall]
display = Marble Hall
floor = floor_slabs
wall = wall_marble
ceiling = ceiling_stone

[crypt_chamber]
display = Crypt Chamber
floor = floor_ancient_stone
wall = wall_stone_30
ceiling = ceiling_stone

[crypt_passage]
display = Crypt Passage
floor = floor_slabs
wall = wall_stone_28
ceiling = ceiling_cracked
